💡 **SUGGESTION: a durability failure still falls through to the master-key prompt loop**

With `return _finishCredential()` the attempts loop now propagates the durability verdict, but `_ensureCredential` cannot distinguish "no dial worked" from "the dial worked but the config lost the secret":

```dart
final cachedEnrolled = await _tryCredentialAttempts(...);
if (cachedEnrolled || await _promptMasterCredential()) return true;
say('could not enroll with this hub — manual recovery: set the hub password ...');
```

In the durability-failure case on an interactive host the user is then prompted up to 3× for the master key (the dial itself already succeeded — re-dialing cannot fix a broken config write), and after those prompts the final line contradicts the durability hint the user just saw ("could not enroll with this hub — set the hub password…" vs "the dial credential did not survive … re-run fa dap start").

Consider short-circuiting when the dial succeeded but the credential could not be made durable — e.g. `_tryCredentialAttempts` returning a distinct outcome (or an `enrolled: bool` + `durable: bool` record) so `_ensureCredential` can return false immediately with only the durability hint. Rare path, so this is polish, not a blocker.

