if (cachedEnrolled || await _promptMasterCredential()) return true;
say('could not enroll with this hub — manual recovery: set the hub password ...');
```

In the durability-failure case on an interactive host the user is then prompted up to 3× for the master key (the dial itself already succeeded — re-dialing cannot fix a broken config write), and after those prompts the final line contradicts the durability hint the user just saw ("could not enroll with this hub — set the hub password…" vs "the dial credential did not survive … re-run fa dap start").

